    </node>
    <node id="GOOD_MATRIX">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Good_Matrix defines the event of achieving a "good matrix," which is a specific configuration of a matrix where the top-left quadrant contains only '1' characters, and the other three quadrants contain only '0' characters. This event is the goal the student's program attempts to achieve.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-076bbe3986a1ac2be6fa34ff30ec0d80</data>
    </node>
    <node id="STUDENT_PROGRAM">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Student_Program represents the student's submitted code, which is a C++ program designed to solve the matrix transformation problem. The program includes a main function that reads input, calls a solve function, and outputs results. The program structure includes standard input-output operations and a control structure for handling multiple test cases. However, the program's logic, particularly in the solve function, does not correctly implement the required matrix transformations.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-076bbe3986a1ac2be6fa34ff30ec0d80</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOLVE_FUNCTION">
