      <data key="d3">78.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Control Structures like if-statements are essential for directing the flow and decisions within the simulation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The control structures implement the simulation logic. The program uses conditions to calculate appropriate values for the matrix elements."&lt;SEP&gt;"No relationship as the Simulation entity is not related to control structures in this context."&lt;SEP&gt;"Control structures implement the simulation by iterating through elements and calculating operation counts."&lt;SEP&gt;"The control structures are used to implement the simulation of matrix transformations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The control structures in the student's program are used to simulate the swaps of characters in the matrix, demonstrating a direct relationship between the logical flow and the physical act of simulation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The control structure (loops and conditions) directly enables the simulation of matrix transformation steps."&lt;SEP&gt;"While the student uses control structures, their implementation does not correctly demonstrate simulation techniques required for the problem solution."&lt;SEP&gt;"The student correctly simulates the query process using control structures to maintain the original array while answering each query."&lt;SEP&gt;"The student implemented control structures well (7 points) but their simulation approach (8 points) for tracking element positions after sorting appears to be the key area needing improvement, as indicated by the partial score."</data>
